.TH "SPEECHSYNTHESISUTTERANCE.END_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SpeechSynthesisUtterance.end_event \- SpeechSynthesisUtterance: end
event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]end\f[B]\f[R] event of the Web Speech API
\f[CR]SpeechSynthesisUtterance\f[R] object is fired when the utterance
has finished being spoken.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqend\(dq, (event) => { })

onend = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]SpeechSynthesisEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
You can use the \f[CR]end\f[R] event in an \f[CR]addEventListener\f[R]
method:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.addEventListener(\(dqend\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(
    \(gaUtterance has finished being spoken after ${event.elapsedTime} seconds.\(ga,
  );
});
.EE
.PP
Or use the \f[CR]onend\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.onend = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(
    \(gaUtterance has finished being spoken after ${event.elapsedTime} seconds.\(ga,
  );
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Web Speech API
